 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Varda's W-1 vehicle after landing in 2024. Photo: Varda/John Kraus

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 💫 Elon Musk reportedly ordered the Starlink connection Ukraine's military relies on to be slowed down, according to the Wall Street Journal .

 Yes, but: Reuters reported a few days earlier that the order came from within the White House. 💭 My thought bubble: There's still a lot of finger pointing and, as Axios' Barak Ravid has reported , the situation was "still unclear" to the Ukrainians last week. 🔎 Varda Space Industries is probing how microgravity could improve a new cancer treatment, my colleague Alex Fitzpatrick reports . 

 Context: "Microgravity lets pharmaceutical compounds crystalize without disruptive processes like sedimentation and convection, potentially leading to better solubility, efficacy and other benefits," Fitzpatrick writes. 💭 My thought bubble: It's a fascinating experiment that weaves together two of the hottest sectors right now, biotech and space. 🇮🇱 The Israel Defense Forces has a new space warfare commander, the Times of Israel reports .

 What they're saying: Israeli Defense Minister Israel Katz said the country's new space division will turn "Israel into a security space power: Star Wars, made in Israel," the newspaper reports. 💭 My thought bubble: Given the heavy use of U.S. space assets in the Middle East, the move isn't surprising. 
 
